<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bora Bora</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bora Bora is a volcanic island with a lagoon and barrier reef in the Leeward group of the Society Islands, in French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polynesia">Polynesia</a>. In the 19th century it was ruled by its own chiefs and kings, rivals of Raiatea and Tahiti. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> annexed it in 1888, adding it to the French Establishments in Oceania.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bora-bora.jpg" alt="Bora Bora" width="320" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA Johnson Space Center · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bora_Bora_ISS006.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
